  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "QR3-001",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "category": "correctness-localization",
      "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Components/Management/Repositories/RepositoryDetailDialog.razor",
      "location": "line 49; supporting mapping at src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/RepositoryProfilingCoordinator.cs lines 830-857 and assertions at tests/Vulgata.Tests/DashboardPanelTests.cs lines 278-282 and 400-412",
      "affected_requirement": "FR-019; Story 4.2 AC-7; repository-scan-overview Chinese UI contract",
      "evidence": "The coordinator serializes FrameworkConfidence with ToString(), producing the canonical English values High or Medium, and the Razor component renders that value directly as user-visible text in 置信度 @framework.StrongestConfidence. The component tests affirm the defect by requiring High. FR-019 requires every new user-visible label, summary, warning, and error to use Simplified Chinese; the overview contract exempts technical facts such as provider language tokens and normalized framework names, but not confidence labels.",
      "correction_outcome": "Keep the API wire values High and Medium where the accepted contract requires them, but map confidence to approved Simplified Chinese display text at the Razor presentation boundary. Update the component tests to require the Chinese confidence value and to reject user-visible English High and Medium so the wire contract and UI localization contract are independently protected."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Full quality review only; this verdict does not substitute for the separate acceptance axis. Correctness: REVISE because the management UI exposes an English confidence enum in a Chinese-only V1 surface. Security: no blocking issue found; provider paths are fail-closed and revalidated, repository visibility is enforced, framework inspection is nonexecuting and bounded, and persisted/logged provider outcomes use safe paths. Edge cases: no additional blocking issue found across rooted, traversal, control-character, unknown-path, malformed-row, duplicate-coordinate, invalid-owner, strict-UTF8, cap, retry, and durable-recovery paths. Test quality: focused provider, profiling, framework, API, and component suites cover the major seams, and retained raw-result hashes and counts match the reconstruction/current-verification ledgers; however, the component tests currently lock in QR3-001 instead of guarding the Chinese rendering contract. Architecture seams: Core contracts, Infrastructure provider/detector/persistence, Web coordination/API/presentation, and embedded catalog responsibilities remain separated with no additional blocking leakage. Migration and persistence: the two migrations are narrow and reversible, the model snapshot matches, and completed profile persistence is transactional with recovery to the durable Profiling state. Regression risk: medium until QR3-001 is corrected because changing enum serialization globally could break the canonical API wire contract; localize only at the presentation boundary and add negative UI regression coverage. Evidence integrity: PASS for the retained evidence inspected; raw result files, recorded lengths and SHA-256 values, source commit/tree ancestry, candidate tree, checkpoint trailer, and exact binary diff hash were independently matched. No candidate-specific test run was performed in this review because the immutable read-only boundary permits only the verdict artifact and dotnet test would write build outputs; the retained evidence explicitly distinguishes its verification commit and does not claim candidate-specific T045/T046 or final-image completion."
